{
  "contract": "Bench v13 per-case gate finding tokens (issue #1852). One list for both sides of the wire: the Go scorer emits these exact strings in CaseScore.catalog.findings (internal/scorer/catalog_gate.go CatalogFinding*), CaseScore.claim_provenance.findings (internal/scoregates/text_provenance.go Finding*) and as bare CaseScore.notes markers (internal/scorer/twins_v13.go TwinNote*); the Platform re-emits only tokens byte-identical to these (apps/platform/ditto/api_models/gate_evidence.py GATE_FINDINGS, pinned by ditto/tests/api_server/endpoints/test_gate_notes.py). `zeroing` is whether the settled finding zeroes the case when its gate runs in enforce; a case carrying one is a would-be zero in shadow. `waived_by` names the finding that, when present on the same case, cancels the zero.",
  "version": 1,
  "findings": {
